{{~!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  blog/head-variant.hbs — resolves a post's head tag to ONE system class.

  Emits a bare class name and nothing else, so it drops into an attribute:

      <header class="ns-posthead {{> "blog/head-variant"}}">

  The blog's counterpart to courses/hero-variant.hbs, and it exists for the
  same reason: the chain is needed three times on a post page (the header
  itself, whether to draw a background layer, whether to draw a cover below
  the meta), and copied three times it would disagree with itself.

  THE TAG CONTRACT — set ONE of these as an internal tag on the post (Ghost
  Admin → the post → Tags → type `#posthead-…`). Internal tags never appear on
  the site, which is why art direction lives in them.

    #posthead-center    centred, cover below the meta line.
                        THE DEFAULT — an untagged post renders this.
    #posthead-wide      left-aligned at the wide measure, cover beside the
                        title. For a piece whose art is worth half the screen.
    #posthead-cover     the feature image full-bleed behind the title,
                        scrimmed. For a photo-led piece.
    #posthead-console   brand navy + the hairline grid. Needs no art at all,
                        and is the house look for an announcement.
    #posthead-minimal   type only, hairline under. For a post with no image —
                        and a blank grey box is worse than no box.

  NO NUMERIC ALIASES HERE, unlike the course hero. The blog never had head
  variants before this — every published post falls to the default, which is
  the centred header it already had. There is nothing to be backwards
  compatible with.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --~}}
{{~#has tag="#posthead-center"}}ns-posthead--center
{{~else has tag="#posthead-wide"}}ns-posthead--wide
{{~else has tag="#posthead-cover"}}ns-posthead--cover
{{~else has tag="#posthead-console"}}ns-posthead--console
{{~else has tag="#posthead-minimal"}}ns-posthead--minimal
{{~else}}ns-posthead--center
{{~/has~}}
